* ============================================================================
* 05_roundtrip_dbf_csv_dbf_v2.dts  --  DBF -> CSV -> DBF, runnable
*
* Replaces 05_roundtrip_dbf_csv_dbf.dts. FOUR of its five lines could not run:
*   EXPORT CSV <f> HEADER ON DATES ISO    -> EXPORT [TO] <file> [CSV|PIPE]
*   IMPORT CSV <f> SCHEMA <j> REJECTS <r> -> IMPORT <csvfile> only
*   USE rt_students                       -> IMPORT appends into the OPEN table
*                                            and never creates rt_students
*   ECHO ... (rows=%LASTCOUNT%)           -> ECHO does NOT expand %LASTCOUNT%;
*                                            it prints the token literally
*                                            (proven by run, 2026-07-26)
* plus _drops/ does not exist.
*
* This is the test the PDLC review cites for "DBF/xBase and CSV conversion:
* empirically demonstrated". Until this version records a run, that line is
* unsupported. See README_SUITE_REPAIR_V1.md.
* ============================================================================

SET TALK ON
ECHO CONV05 BEGIN roundtrip

* -- leg 1: build the origin DBF from sealed source ---------------------------
ECHO CONV05 ORIGIN
AUTODBF X64 ROUNDTRIP_ORIGIN_ITEMS_V1 FROM cascade_precision_erp/data/Items.csv HEADER INFER OVERWRITE
USE ROUNDTRIP_ORIGIN_ITEMS_V1
COUNT
STRUCT

* -- leg 2: DBF -> CSV ---------------------------------------------------------
ECHO CONV05 EXPORT
EXPORT TO tmp/conv05_roundtrip.csv CSV

* -- leg 3: CSV -> DBF ---------------------------------------------------------
ECHO CONV05 RETURN
AUTODBF X64 ROUNDTRIP_RETURN_ITEMS_V1 FROM tmp/conv05_roundtrip.csv HEADER INFER OVERWRITE
USE ROUNDTRIP_RETURN_ITEMS_V1
COUNT
STRUCT

* -- leg 4: value-level equivalence -------------------------------------------
* Shape equality is necessary, not sufficient. Compare the same record on both
* sides: the empty LIST_PRICE is the one most likely to be damaged by a round
* trip, because an empty numeric can plausibly come back as 0.
ECHO CONV05 COMPARE origin
USE ROUNDTRIP_ORIGIN_ITEMS_V1
LOCATE FOR SKU = "RAW-SHAFT-4140"
DISPLAY
ECHO CONV05 COMPARE return
USE ROUNDTRIP_RETURN_ITEMS_V1
LOCATE FOR SKU = "RAW-SHAFT-4140"
DISPLAY

ECHO CONV05 END

* ============================================================================
* PASS CRITERIA
*   origin COUNT  = 18   and  return COUNT  = 18
*   origin fields = 13   and  return fields = 13
*   the two DISPLAY blocks are IDENTICAL field for field, in particular:
*     STANDARD_COST = 48.0  on both sides
*     LIST_PRICE    = EMPTY on both sides  (NOT 0 on the return leg)
*     CATEGORY      = Raw Metal            (embedded space survives CSV)
*
* KNOWN-UNKNOWN, record honestly on first run:
*   Type letters on the return leg are inferred from what EXPORT wrote, not from
*   the sealed CSV. If EXPORT renders a numeric differently than the original
*   (trailing .0, padding, scientific form) the return leg may infer a different
*   width or even a different letter. Any divergence is a REAL EXPORT-FIDELITY
*   FINDING. Record it; do not tune the expectation to make it green.
*
* ============================================================================
* FIRST RECORDED RUN -- 2026-07-26, build Jul 26 2026 12:52:47, v0.6
* Invocation: ./datarun.ps1 -CommandLines 'DOTSCRIPT <abs path>' > tmp\conv05.txt
* ============================================================================
* RESULT: PASS -- LOSSLESS ROUND TRIP.
*
*   origin  : 18 rows, 13 fields
*   EXPORT  : "Exported 18 records to tmp/conv05_roundtrip.csv"
*   return  : 18 rows, 13 fields
*
*   STRUCTURE IDENTICAL ON BOTH LEGS -- not merely the same type letters, but
*   the same widths and decimal counts, field for field:
*     N(2,0) C(16) C(30) C(4) C(10) C(10) N(6,2) N(5,1) N(5,1) N(5,1) N(2,0)
*     C(17) N(1,0)
*   The KNOWN-UNKNOWN above did NOT materialise: EXPORT rendered every value so
*   that re-inference reproduced the origin schema exactly. That is a stronger
*   result than the test required -- export fidelity is round-trip stable.
*
*   VALUE COMPARISON: the two DISPLAY blocks are identical field for field.
*     STANDARD_COST = 48.0        on both legs
*     LIST_PRICE    = (empty)     on both legs -- did NOT become 0
*     CATEGORY      = Raw Metal   embedded space survived CSV both ways
*
*   Both tables opened as (v64) with a valid CDX.
*
*   One cosmetic difference, not a defect: the return leg's AUTODBF plan omits
*   the source='...' annotations, because the exported CSV headers already match
*   the normalised x64 names. The 10-char descriptors (DESCRIPTIO, COST_METHO,
*   STANDARD_C, REORDER_PO, REORDER_QT) are identical on both legs.
*
* THIS IS THE EVIDENCE THE PDLC REVIEW WAS MISSING. The line
* "DBF/xBase and CSV conversion: empirically demonstrated" is now supported by a
* preserved transcript -- for the DBF <-> CSV portion. SQLite legs remain gaps.
* ============================================================================
